e.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Working as</b>, at the top of every page, lists every role you have. The one you are in is black; press another to work in it. Your staff functions are there too, as before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Pages of your other roles</b>, under it, goes straight to the most used pages of a role you are not in right now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Signing in opens the role you used last on this device.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">What you may open has not changed: each page still checks your role.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-possible-wrong-person-at-pickup" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Possible wrong person at pickup</h2><p class="gd-p">At a pickup, staff (and a renter checking in alone) can take a photo of the licence the person is holding. It is compared with the licence and selfie on file (name, licence number, expiry and face), and the card shown is compared with the card on file by its last four digits and its name. The card is never photographed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A mismatch raises an urgent To do, <b class="gd-ui">Possible wrong person at pickup</b>, for Fleet and for Admin (Fleet sees it on To do), with what did not match, and a staff alert. The booking page shows the same mark at the top, with each line of the check.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Review the licence</b> on the booking: the photos taken at the pickup are listed with the licence and selfie on file. Press <b class="gd-ui">View</b> on each to compare them side by side.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Call the staff member at the car if the keys have not been handed over. Finish the To do once you have looked: the mark on the booking goes with it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On a rental covered by the renter&#39;s credit card, a card that is not in the renter&#39;s own name is also raised as <b class="gd-ui">Coverage problem at pickup</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The check is optional and never stops a handover by itself. Every check, matched or not, is kept as evidence and goes into the dispute pack.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-my-rewards-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">My rewards (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">My rewards</b> is on To do and in the menu under My numbers. It shows your discount, your tier and your free rental days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Rental perks are for in-person staff in Canada. If you work remotely or outside Canada, the card says there are no rental perks on your account, because you cannot rent here.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">From the day your academy and your agreement are done you get 15% off your own rentals. Your code is on the page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Sales: you earn 1 free rental day for every 100 rental days you book. Book 50 rental days in a month for <b class="gd-ui">Silver</b> (20% off) and 100 for <b class="gd-ui">Gold</b> (25% off and 1 bonus free day that month). A tier lasts through the next month. The month&#39;s top seller gets a free weekend.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">To use free days, press <b class="gd-ui">Get a free-day code</b>, choose how many days, and use the code on one rental. A free day ends 6 months after you earn it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The rules: you must be the driver; not on exotic or partner cars; the pickup is within 48 hours of booking and never on dates a renter has asked for; free days go on CarmaCars&#39; own cars first.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-choose-your-notifications-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Choose your notifications (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>, under <b class="gd-ui">Notification preferences</b>, lists each kind of notification we send you, with a switch for <b class="gd-ui">Push</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Email</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>. A switch is saved the moment you move it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">How often</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Instant</b> sends each one as it happens. <b class="gd-ui">Daily summary</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Weekly summary</b> holds the optional emails and sends them as one email in the morning.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Quiet hours</b>: turn them on and set the times. Optional phone alerts and texts wait until the quiet hours end.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Turn every optional notification off</b> stops them all at once. You still see every message in your portal.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The kinds under <b class="gd-ui">Always on</b> cannot be switched off: security and sign-in codes, agreement notices, pay statements, the work assigned to you, and onboarding, access and suspension notices.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">If a text cannot be sent, the same message comes by email instead, so nothing is lost.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-guide-me" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Guide me</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Guide me</b> walks you through a real job step by step while you do it, on the real screens. It is off until you want it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Guide me</b> at the top of any page and choose the job: send an offer to a renter, answer a booking request, record an e-Transfer or another payment, a return handover and deposit review, approve an owner&#39;s car (the ones of your functions). Or press <b class="gd-ui">Guide me through this</b> on the page itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A small card points at the next thing to fill or press, with one instruction and Step X of Y. Do it: the card moves on by itself once it is really done. <b class="gd-ui">Back</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Skip</b> and the cross (exit) are always there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">It follows you from page to page in the job, and picks up where you were if you leave and come back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Tick <b class="gd-ui">Keep Guide me on</b> in its menu: on the first page of a job it offers to walk you through it. Untick it to stop.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'start-here', 'start', null, '### Who this guide is for

CarmaCars field staff: drivers, detailers, and drivers who also detail. You hand cars over, take them back, move them and shoot listing photos. Everything is on your phone. Your jobs are under **Field work** in the staff portal; if you also hold another function (Sales, for example), its pages are in the same menu.

### What you need

- Your phone, charged, with a data connection (photos and signatures save as you take them)
- The invitation email from CarmaCars (the link works for 24 hours)
- A car charger and a cloth for the camera lens

## Once you are hired

You are not working a shift right away. First your training (the academy), then you claim your shifts online in the portal.

1. Say hello in the team chat: the CarmaCars Team WhatsApp group (the link is in your portal once your agreement is signed and the academy is passed).
2. In each WhatsApp group you are in, set your member tag as "Name - Position", for example "Ali - Field".

## Your first sign-in

1. Open the invitation email on your phone and press its link within 24 hours. Choose a password and press **Save the new password**.
2. You land on **Today**. Next time, sign in at `carmacars.ca/sign-in` with your Email and Password.
3. In your browser''s menu, choose **Add to Home Screen**. The portal then opens full screen, like an app.
4. Open **Profile**, add your mobile number and press **Save my phone**.
5. At the top of the page, fill in your Home address and Postal code and press **Save my home address**. You need it before you add a rental or earn a commission.

![](/guides/img/field-04-profile-phone-f05000e2.jpg "phone; size: 390 920; pins: 4 92.3 78.3")

> Good to know: Recommended: on Profile, press **Set up two-step sign-in** and follow the steps with an authenticator app.

## Stuck on a page?

If you work on a page for a few minutes without anything saving, see the same error three times, or go back and forth between the same two steps, a small box asks **Need a hand with** the page. **Open the guide section** opens this guide at the right chapter in a sheet from the bottom of the screen; **Back to what I was doing** closes it and everything you typed is still there. **Open the Academy lesson** opens the lesson in a new tab. **Not now** quiets it on that page for a day. It never shows while a renter signs.

> Good to know: When we update our terms of use, our privacy policy or an agreement you signed with us, the next time you open your portal it shows **We''ve updated our terms**: a short summary of what changed and the new text. Tick that you read it and press **Accept** to continue. It does not change an agreement you already signed or a past booking.

## Your first days

Your portal opens in order: your staff agreement first, then the academy (Training), then your jobs. Welcome shows each step and asks for the name you go by. Once both are done, Welcome and Today show the team''s WhatsApp group: join it, then press **I joined**.

## The weekly townhall (release 35)

Every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time, and everyone attends. Open **Townhall**: **Join the call** there, or **Check in** from 15 minutes before, counts you as there. You get a reminder an hour before.

## Report a bug (release 37)
Something not working? Press **Report a bug** at the top of any page. A picture of the page is taken first (passwords and card fields are hidden); write what happened (at least 30 characters), what you expected and the steps if you know them, choose how bad it is (**Blocks my work** alerts the Admins at once) and add or paste more pictures. The page, your browser and its recent errors go with it. **My bug reports** shows each report and its status: new, being looked at, fixed or won''t fix.

## The weekly townhall card (release 41)

From the day before the weekly townhall until it ends, your home page shows the **Townhall** card: the day and time (Toronto), a countdown, **Join / check in** (it opens 15 minutes before; joining through it checks you in), **Add to calendar**, and a red line if you missed the last townhall: one more miss locks your account. You also get a reminder the day before at 10:00 am, the morning of at 9:00 am, an hour before, and 15 minutes before with the join link.

## Work chats only

All work communication happens in the group work chats (the CarmaCars Team and Sales WhatsApp groups, and the chats in the portal), never in private messages. Questions, handovers, problems and customer details go in the group, so the whole team sees them and nothing is lost when someone is away. If a colleague or an Admin writes to you privately about work, answer in the group.
## Something to check on your record (release 48)

When something on your record looks wrong, a box opens on any page of the portal and says exactly what, with the box to fix it right there: your staff agreement waiting for your driver''s licence number or home address, a home address outside Ontario while you work in person in Toronto (fix it, or press It''s correct and say why), a licence that expires within 30 days (or has expired), pay details missing, a phone number that is not valid, or your WhatsApp member tag not confirmed. Press **Save** and the box checks again.

1. Your agreement waiting for something you give cannot be put off: once you save it, the agreement is made and appears under Documents to sign at once. The sign page says the same when nothing is ready to sign yet.
2. Anything else you can put off with **Remind me later**: it comes back after a day.
